From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:04:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 431/443] [ae-patch] Fix the check findings on 0430: use the
 computed turn state for the refresh, withdraw the notice only on an explicit
 off marker

The every 20th prompt refresh read the saved full_in_turn flag instead of the value that accounts for an interrupt, so an interrupted turn still delayed it by one prompt. The withdrawal line no longer comes from an empty or missing context file, which a pane-typed, queued or system prompt can produce while the notice is on: the server attaches an explicit off block only when it has no team notice, the Claude executor turns it into a marker line in the context file, and the hook withdraws a sent notice only on that marker. The executor no longer writes an empty context file.
